# The interactive site under docs/ is hand-authored presentation and data code.
#
# It is NOT ignored to dodge formatting - it is ignored because reformatting it
# destroys things prettier has no way to understand:
#
#   app.js      - 1200 lines of template literals with hand-placed newlines that
#                 line up quiz options and mock-exam chrome. Prettier reflows
#                 them and the rendered HTML whitespace shifts.
#   style.css   - one declaration per line, grouped by visual layer. Prettier
#                 collapses it to as few lines as possible, which defeats the
#                 grouping and makes the diff for a real style change unreadable.
#   curriculum.js / answers.js - large curated data literals (100KB+). A prettier
#                 pass produces a 10,000-line diff for a one-line content fix.
#
# These files are still checked, just by the tool that suits them:
#   node --check docs/assets/*.js     (syntax)
#   scripts/validate-metadata.js      (manifest/force-app consistency)
#   scripts/check-site-data.js        (curriculum/answers schema + cross-refs)
docs/

